title: importing an exported vault back
pid: b32ce09e-977f-4fec-b957-3b408a24e77d
body: |2-
  : cargo run --bin skg -- import-obsidian VAULT-DIR OUT-DIR
  reads a vault that =export-obsidian= wrote back into =.skg= files,
  writing each skgrepo folder its =README.md= lists to the folder of
  that name in =OUT-DIR=, which must be absent or empty. It refuses a
  vault whose =skg-format= is not the one it reads. It needs no server and
  touches no configured skgrepo; it reads IDs from block IDs, properties
  and comments, and mints none. Importing an export gives back the
  skgrepo's files as skg writes them, byte for byte, and exporting that
  import gives back the vault; the tests check both on
  =skg-system/= and on random skgrepos. It reads only what the exporter
  writes, and stops at the first line it cannot place, naming its file
  and line, so it is not yet a way to read notes written in Obsidian.
